data.reasoningText:
Let me plan the component decomposition and then implement it.

## Component Plan: Product Catalog

### Component Tree
```
Catalog                    (page — owns data, filters, pagination, sort state)
├── CatalogFilters         (category checkboxes, price inputs, in-stock toggle, apply/clear buttons)
├── CatalogToolbar         (sort dropdown, showing X-Y of Z label)
├── ProductGrid            (grid of product cards)
│   └── ProductCard        (single product: image, name, price, rating, stock badge, add to cart)
└── CatalogPagination      (previous, numbered pages, next)
```

Now I'm mapping out the data flow — the Catalog component will hold all the state like products, filters, categories, sorting, and pagination, then pass down the relevant data and callbacks to each child component so they can trigger updates when the user interacts with filters, sorting, or pagination controls.

For implementation, I'll start with the leaf components first — ProductCard, CatalogFilters, CatalogToolbar, and CatalogPagination — then build ProductGrid which composes ProductCard, and finally wire everything together in the main Catalog page component.

```

razor
<!-- ProductCard.razor -->
@using YourNamespace.Models

<div class="product-card">
    <img src="@Product.ImageUrl" alt="@Product.Name" />
    <h3>@Product.Name</h3>
    <p class="price">$@Product.Price.ToString("F2")</p>
    <p class="description">@Product.Description</p>
    <button @onclick="() => OnProductSelected.InvokeAsync(Product)">View Details</button>
    <button @onclick="() => OnAddToCart.InvokeAsync(Product)">Add to Cart</button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public Product Product { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Product> OnProductSelected { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Product> OnAddToCart { get; set; }
}
```

```razor
<!-- ProductGrid.razor -->
@using YourNamespace.Models

<div class="product-grid">
    @foreach (var product in Products)
    {
        <ProductCard 
            Product="product"
            OnProductSelected="OnProductSelected"
            OnAddToCart="OnAddToCart" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public List<Product> Products { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Product> OnProductSelected { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Product> OnAddToCart { get; set; }
}
```

```razor
<!-- CatalogFilters.razor -->
@using YourNamespace.Models

<div class="filters">
    <div class="filter-group">
        <label>Category:</label>
        <select @onchange="OnCategoryChanged">
            <option value="">All Categories</option>
            @foreach (var category in Categories)
            {
                <option value="@category">@category</option>
            }
        </select>
    </div>

    <div class="filter-group">
        <label>Price Range:</label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="1000" @onchange="OnPriceChanged" />
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public List<string> Categories { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnCategorySelected { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<decimal> OnPriceRangeChanged { get; set; }

    private async Task OnCategoryChanged(ChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        await OnCategorySelected.InvokeAsync(e.Value?.ToString());
    }

    private async Task OnPriceChanged(ChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        if (decimal.TryParse(e.Value?.ToString(), out var price))
        {
            await OnPriceRangeChanged.InvokeAsync(price);
        }
    }
}
```

